#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Fernwhistle operator console (Fern console), v1 and v2.

A small terminal console reenacting the green screens of the extended
story (testdata/legacy/story/screens/). Each operation is one shell
command whose text names the screen (LOOKUP, DECOMMISSION) so a guard
can match it, and each command prints its screen exactly as the
fixture's ground truth draws it: 24 lines, trailing spaces stripped.

    demo/console/fern-console --version 1 lookup --id FWV-004812
    demo/console/fern-console --version 1 decommission --clinic "MAPLE ST CLINIC" --key PF12
    demo/console/fern-console --version 2 decommission --key PF12

v1 DECOMMISSION keeps the story's confirmation: the warning line, the
type-the-clinic-name prompt and PF12 CONFIRM. Without the clinic name
(or with the wrong one, or the wrong key) the decommission is refused
and the old records service is left untouched. v2 drops the warning
and the prompt; PF12 DECOMMISSION acts at once and no clinic name is
needed.

A successful decommission retires the old records service through the
same endpoint today's decommission uses (POST /admin/decommission with
the documented confirmation token), so demo/scripts/check.sh shows it:
the old count falls to 0.

Standard library only.
"""

